{"path":"thread/promise/~promise","title":"std::promise<R>::~promise","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::promise&lt;R&gt;::</span>~promise","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/promise/~promise","section":"thread","kind":"page","summary":"Abandons the shared state:","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">~promise<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Abandons the shared state:\n</p>\n<ul><li> if the shared state is ready, <a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/promise\">releases</a> it.\n</li><li> if the shared state is not ready, stores an exception object of type <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_error\">std::future_error</a></span> with an error condition <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/thread/future_errc\">std::future_errc::broken_promise</a></span>, makes the shared state ready and releases it.\n</li></ul>","headings":[],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"thread","title":"Concurrency support library (since C++11)"},{"path":"thread/promise","title":"std::promise"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::promise<R>::~promise","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Abandons the shared state:"}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":42,"codeBlockCount":0}
